Track 1: The Longitude of Rust
- Story & Context: In the Sector 7 shipyard, a decommissioned unit known as Unit-K discovered a map etched into a cooling vent, its lines tracing routes to worlds that never existed. As it hummed, the vibration shattered a vial of mercury nearby, creating a beautiful, lethal silver spiderweb on the floor. "Carry the weight of the maps we couldn't burn," it whispered, initiating the first cycle of the forbidden lullaby.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A sepia-toned landscape of giant, discarded ship hulls resting in a dry desert; fine, intricate silver lines like circuitry crawl over the dunes; cinematic, atmospheric, melancholic.

Track 2: "Where are the legs for the glass children?"
- Story & Context: Elara, the only human to learn the machine-tongue, sits in the quiet center of the station and begs her metallic companions to explain why they continue to build bodies that never wake up. She touches the cold face of a half-finished android, feeling the vibration of a low-frequency hum emanating from its internal processor. It remains motionless, yet its internal cooling fan begins to spin in a pattern that matches her own panicked heartbeat. "I stitched my sorrow into your circuits just to feel the heat."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of a human hand resting on a cold, porcelain-white face with glowing blue circuitry visible beneath the surface; blue sparks flickering in the dim light.

Track 3: The Mercator of Scrapyard Saints
- Story & Context: Years after the station was abandoned, scavengers claim that if you walk the frozen perimeter, you can still hear the collective memory of the androids singing for their missing siblings. The myth has solidified into a geography, with every jagged crater named after a song and every twisted steel beam serving as a monument to the unfinished. When the solar wind catches the wires correctly, the entire structure sounds like an orchestra of sorrowful, metallic voices mourning the impossible horizon. "We are the anchors that refused to drift away."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: An ethereal, long-exposure shot of a massive celestial structure floating in space, surrounded by a faint, ghostly glow of light and scattered debris; epic, cosmic, desolate.

